{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"reasoning","text":"Now the results look much more reasonable:\n- 968 candidates, 26 stop_gained, scattered across many genes.\n- FINAL: chr9:131263558 A>G FAM78A stop_gained AF=0.3307 (84/254) p.(Tyr78Ter)\n\nBut wait — I need to scrutinize the candidates:\n1. FAM78A chr9:131263558 A>G AF=0.33, 84/254. But FAM78A also has two other low-frequency candidates: chr9:131263507 G>A AF=0.045 and chr9:131263572 C>T AF=0.03. Multiple candidates within the same gene — hmm, the AF 0.33 one is dominant. The AF 0.045/0.03 ones might be errors or artifacts.\n2. FAM78A — is this \"highly LoF-intolerant\"? FAM78A (family with sequence similarity 78 member A)… not a classic haploinsufficient gene. Hmm. gnomAD LOEUF for FAM78A? Unknown, probably mid-range. This needs checking.\n3. Other interesting candidates:\n   - STXBP1 chr9:127661125 G>T AF=0.1935 — STXBP1 is highly LoF-intolerant (LOEUF ~0.05, pLI 1.0, epileptic encephalopathy)!\n   - ENG chr9:127811261 G>A AF=0.119 — ENG is LoF-intolerant (HHT, haploinsufficiency).\n   - GRIN3A chr9:101670953 C>T AF=0.5517 — AF>0.5.\n   - C5 AF=0.5254/0.0495/0.0309, ALAD AF=0.5714 (AF>0.5 is suspicious — could be a strand or paralog issue, or could be a genuine het with a reference bias… actually, if it's germline het, AF 0.5–0.57 is reasonable).\n   - LAMC3 AF=0.16/0.12 (two candidates).\n\nHmm, the current selection is picking FAM78A because alt_reads=84 is the largest. But \"high confidence mosaic nonsense SNV in a highly LoF-intolerant gene\" — FAM78A might not qualify as \"highly LoF-intolerant\". The true target could be STXBP1 (AF 0.19) or ENG (AF 0.12).\n\nNeed to run co-occurrence + read-level QC to distinguish the true mosaic variant from artifacts. The co-occurrence test will tell us which candidate's alt reads are clean.\n\nAlso note: FAM78A has three candidates in one gene (0.33, 0.045, 0.03) — if they co-occur on the same reads, they're a paralog artifact (or a mismatched hap