{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"reasoning","text":"While co-occur is running (about 2.5 minutes), let me think about gnomAD constraint metrics for candidate genes (from knowledge):\n\n- STXBP1 (chr9q34.11): LOEUF ≈ 0.05–0.06, pLI = 1.0. Highly LoF-intolerant. Haploinsufficiency causes STXBP1 encephalopathy.\n- ENG (chr9q34.11): LOEUF ≈ 0.19? pLI ≈ 1.0. Haploinsufficiency → HHT1. Highly intolerant.\n- FAM78A: unknown / poorly characterized. Probably not highly constrained (LOEUF around 0.5–0.8?).\n- GRIN3A: moderately constrained (LOEUF around 0.2?).\n- C5: AR complement deficiency — pLI is low.\n- ALAD: AR (porphyria) — pLI is low.\n- BAG1: moderate.\n- LAMC3: moderate?\n- GLT6D1: ?\n- COL27A1: ?\n- SEC16A: ?\n- ANKRD18A/B: low constraint?\n- RALGPS1: ?\n- OR13D1: OR gene, low constraint.\n- PAEP: ?\n- GLDC: AR glycine encephalopathy (some forms), pLI is low.\n- PTPA: ?\n\nTherefore the candidates for \"highly LoF-intolerant\" are: STXBP1 and ENG (both in the chr9q34.11 region!), possibly also GRIN3A.\n\nNote: STXBP1 and ENG are adjacent in chr9q34.11 (~127.6–127.8 Mb). Two candidates in this region — hmm, interesting. Could it be a mosaic deletion? No — these are SNVs.\n\nWait, actually — both STXBP1 chr9:127661125 G>T AF=0.19 and ENG chr9:127811261 G>A AF=0.119 — if they were on the same mosaic haplotype, they'd co-occur on reads... but they're 150 kb apart, so they'd never be on the same read. Co-occurrence analysis won't link them.\n\nHmm, but if there's one true mosaic nonsense variant, which one is it? Let me think: the task says \"high-confidence mosaic nonsense SNV\" (singular). The decoys might be low-level artifacts (AF ~0.05–0.2 from mapping errors), and the true variant would have clean supporting reads.\n\nFAM78A AF=0.33 has the highest alt count (84), but there are 2 other low-AF candidates within the same gene. If those co-occur with the AF=0.33 variant on reads, it's suspicious (paralog). The co-occurrence analysis will reveal