{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_82","type":"reasoning","text":"This makes everything completely clear:\n\n**FAM78A (chr9:131263xxx)**: A massive cluster of dozens of candidate variants at depth 100–800×, AF from 0.02–0.5, all with clean_frac ≈ 0, mean_other_alleles ≈ 2. This is a classic paralog/pseudogene mismapping artifact (or a highly diverged haplotype region). The FAM78A AF=0.331 \"stop_gained\" has clean_frac=0.0 — all 84 alt reads also carry about 2.4 other candidate alleles. Definitely an artifact. Good thing I checked!\n\n**STXBP1 chr9:127661125 G>T AF=0.194**: depth=93, carriers=18, clean_frac=1.0, other=0.0, strand 14/4. All 18 alt reads carry only this allele and nothing else. Clean mosaic signal at about 19% AF in STXBP1 — a gene known to be highly LoF-intolerant (LOEUF ~0.05, pLI=1.0, haploinsufficiency causes developmental and epileptic encephalopathy).\n\nOther clean stop_gained:\n- C5 AF=0.525 (clean, but AF≈0.5 = heterozygous germline; C5 is not LoF-intolerant)\n- ALAD AF=0.571 (clean, AF>0.5, strong strand bias 2/18 — suspicious; ALAD is not LoF-intolerant; AF 0.57 is odd)\n- GRIN3A AF=0.552 (clean, AF≈0.55 ≈ heterozygous; GRIN3A has moderate constraint, but AF is not in the mosaic range)\n- COL27A1 AF=0.143 (clean but only 4 carriers, all reverse strand 0/4 — weak, single-strand; COL27A1 is not known as highly LoF-intolerant)\n\nDirty stop candidates (artifacts): FAM78A, RALGPS1, OR13D1, PAEP, LAMC3, ANKRD18A/B, GLT6D1, BAG1, C9orf85, ENG (clean_frac 0.35), PTPA, SEC16A, GLDC, C5(0.05), FAM78A's lower-AF ones.\n\nAlso interesting: CEL has two clean non-stop candidates at AF 0.185/0.249 (synonymous + missense) — hmm, these are also clean and mosaic-range AF. But they're not nonsense. Probably another mosaic event (or a simulated second haplotype block?). Not relevant to our task (nonsense SNV only). Hmm wait — actually interesting: CEL chr9:133069137 C>T AF=0.185 (58 carriers, clean 1.0) and chr9:133069199 C>T AF=0.249 (55 carriers, clean 1.0). Two clean mosaic variants 62 bp apart in CEL. Hmm — could CEL also have a mosaic haplotype with two variants? If so, reads carrying one should also carry the other — but co-occurrence says they're clean (each read carries only one of them)… 62 bp apart — a 150 bp read can span both. clean_frac=1.0 means no read carries both. So they're on different reads — two independent mosaic lineages? Or one is an artifact… In any case, not nonsense; irrelevant.\n\nSo the answer: **chr9:127661125 G>T in STXBP1, stop_gained, AF ≈ 0.19 (18/93)**.\n\nWait, but I need to double-check the strand counts: 14 forward / 4 reverse. Some imbalance but both strands present (binomial p-value for 14/18 ≈ 0.03… hmm, borderline. Let me compute: P(X≥14 or X≤4) with n=18, p=0.5 = 2*P(X≤4) = 2*(C(18,0)+C(18,1)+C(18,2)+C(18,3)+C(18,4))/2^18 = 2*(1+18+153+816+3060)/262144 = 2*4048/262144 = 0.0309. Just barely passes at the 0.05 level, but doesn't pass stricter thresholds. Hmm.) Still, 14 fwd + 4 rev is acceptable as supporting evidence.\n\nHmm, but wait — why does STXBP1's depth=93 differ from the pileup's carriers=18? Pileup alt_reads=18? In analysis.py's output: STXBP1 AF=0.1935, and cooccur says depth=93 carriers=18 → AF=18/93=0.194 ✓ consistent (pileup alt count matches cooccur's carrier count — excellent cross-validation).\n\nBut hmm — depth 93 at the STXBP1 position vs. STXBP1's average CDS depth of 62.0 — reasonable.\n\nNext, let me also verify that the STXBP1 position isn't in a problematic context:\n- Check the codon: G>T at chr9:127661125 → p.? Let me get the HGVS from annotation. analysis.py's summary only printed FINAL (FAM78A). Need the STXBP1 annotation details: which transcript, codon change, p.(Xxx). From evidence.json's stop_gained_candidates — but that's from the run where FAM78A was FINAL. The stop candidate list contains annotations for all 26 items — let me extract the STXBP1 entry.\n\nAlso:\n- Verify the reference base G at 127661125 in GRCh38 chr9.\n- Confirm STXBP1's strand and reading frame.\n- Re-check: could this be the natural stop codon position? No — a stop_gained annotation requires that the reference codon isn't a stop.\n\nOne more sanity check: look at read-level evidence for STXBP1 from analysis.py's pass 2 (it was included in collect) — alt read base qualities, mismatches. In the current output/evidence.json, final_variant=FAM78A (wrong), but stop_gained_candidates contains annotations; the read-level evidence is only saved for FINAL. Re-run analysis.py with improved selection (clean read-aware), and the correct final variant will be output along with complete evidence.\n\nNow, how should I incorporate \"clean_frac\" into analysis.py (the deliverable pipeline)? The current selection picks the maximum alt_reads → wrong (FAM78A). Need to integrate co-occurrence-based filtering into analysis.py:\n\nPipeline v2:\n1. Pass 1: pileup → candidates (unchanged).\n2. Pass 2 (all candidates): for each candidate, compute carriers, clean count, strand counts, mean base quality of alt reads, mismatches of alt reads (excluding the variant position itself? no — total mismatches is fine).\n3. Scoring/filtering for high-confidence mosaic:\n   - clean_frac ≥ 0.8 (alt reads carry no other candidate alleles)\n   - alt_reads (carriers) ≥ 5\n   - AF in [0.05, 0.95]… for \"mosaic\": AF < 0.5? Hmm, mosaic can be up to about 0.5, but strictly < 0.5. AF 0.194 ✓. Don't over-restrict: require AF ≤ 0.45 for mosaic interpretation, but keep 0.02–0.98 for candidate detection and document it.\n   - Both strands present (alt_fwd ≥ 1 and alt_rev ≥ 1)? STXBP1 passes (14/4).\n   - Mean base quality of alt ≥ 25?\n   - Then prioritize: stop_gained consequence.\n4. Among clean stop_gained candidates: pick the one with the most alt reads / best AF evidence → STXBP1.\n\nAlso incorporate the LoF-intolerant gene criterion: hardcode a small table of gnomAD v2.1.1 LOEUF/pLI values for relevant genes (documented as external prior knowledge from gnomAD). STXBP1 LOEUF ≈ 0.05 (extremely low = highly LoF-intolerant), pLI=1.0.\n\nActually, let me double-check the exact LOEUF value I remember for STXBP1: gnomAD v2.1.1 constraint metrics — STXBP1: exp_lof ≈ 145, obs_lof ≈ 7? LOEUF = obs/exp upper-bound ratio… STXBP1's LOEUF is about 0.05–0.08. pLI = 1.0. Cite approximately: LOEUF ≈ 0.05, pLI = 1.0 (gnomAD v2.1.1). Should be careful to note these as approximate published values.\n\nAlso confirm that STXBP1 is a protein-coding gene with high LoF intolerance — yes: STXBP1 encephalopathy (OMIM #612164, \"Mental retardation, autosomal dominant 4\" / developmental and epileptic encephalopathy 4) is caused by heterozygous LoF variants; STXBP1 is one of the most constrained genes (LOEUF is among the lowest genome-wide).\n\nOK, implementation of pass 2 in analysis.py (replacing the limited pass 2 evidence collection):\n- Collect for all candidates (968 positions): per-read: base at each overlapping candidate position (Q≥20), and for reads carrying the alt allele: record strand, base quality, mismatches (nmm), votes.\n- Aggregate: carriers, clean, strand +/-, sum bq, sum nmm.\n- Also per-candidate co-occurrence summary.\n- Then selection logic + write output.\n\nMemory/time: pass 2 for 968 candidates — the same as cooccur (about 2.5–3 min). No problem.\n\nRe-check the COL27A1 candidate (4 carriers, all reverse strand) too — excluded by min carriers ≥5 and strand requirements.\n- C5 AF 0.525, ALAD AF 0.571, GRIN3A AF 0.552: AF > 0.5 → heterozygous germline, not mosaic; also genes are not highly LoF-intolerant. If we restrict mosaic AF to < 0.5, these are excluded. Hmm — but is it safe to exclude AF > 0.5 for mosaic? Mosaic variant AF is (in theory) at most 0.5 (heterozygous in all cells). AF 0.52–0.57 suggests germline heterozygosity + noise. The task states mosaic — so AF should be < 0.5. STXBP1 AF=0.194 ✓ clearly mosaic.\n\nNext, HGVS / codon check for STXBP1 chr9:127661125 G>T:\nLet me extract the annotation for this candidate from evidence.json (from the last run). Then finalize.\n\nAlso — one more important verification: BLAST-style verification of the specificity of STXBP1 alt reads: extract several alt reads and confirm they match the STXBP1 reference perfectly except for the variant. Also verify there are no nearly identical paralogous sequences of this exon elsewhere on chr9 (search for the exon sequence with a few mismatches). Let me do this check in the verification script:\n1. Take the reference window around 127661125 (e.g., 300 bp).\n2. Slide across chr9, count positions with ≥95% identity over 150 bp — see if any other locus matches (a paralog would show up).\n3. Print a few alt reads and their alignments.\n\nFirst, let me extract the STXBP1 annotation from evidence.json."}}
